  "theorem_name": "GoldbachPrimePowerCollisionSupportHasDensityZero",
  "declared_proposition": "Let Q be the odd proper-prime-power part of Lambda and let C(X)={even N<=X:(Q*Q)(N)>0}. Then |C(X)|=o(X). Indeed the number A(X) of odd proper prime powers is O(sqrt(X)/log(X)+X^(1/3)log(X))=O(sqrt(X)/log(X)), and every collision-supported target is a sum of two such powers, so |C(X)|<=A(X)^2=O(X/log(X)^2). Consequently the exact TICKET-196 overlap subtraction changes the old union envelope only on a density-zero set of even targets.",
  "mathematical_argument": "For exponent two there are pi(sqrt X) choices. For exponents at least three, summing pi(X^(1/e)) over e<=log_3 X gives O(X^(1/3)log X). The standard Chebyshev prime-counting bound pi(y)=O(y/log y) gives A(X)=O(sqrt X/log X). The addition map from ordered proper-power pairs onto collision-supported targets gives |C(X)|<=A(X)^2. Dividing by the number of even targets proves density zero. Outside C(X), Q*Q(N)=0 exactly, so the corrected and uncorrected envelopes coincide.",
  "reproducible_computation": {
    "theorem": "Let Q be the odd proper-prime-power part of Lambda and let C(X)={even N<=X:(Q*Q)(N)>0}. Then |C(X)|=o(X). Indeed the number A(X) of odd proper prime powers is O(sqrt(X)/log(X)+X^(1/3)log(X))=O(sqrt(X)/log(X)), and every collision-supported target is a sum of two such powers, so |C(X)|<=A(X)^2=O(X/log(X)^2). Consequently the exact TICKET-196 overlap subtraction changes the old union envelope only on a density-zero set of even targets.",
    "proof": "For exponent two there are pi(sqrt X) choices. For exponents at least three, summing pi(X^(1/e)) over e<=log_3 X gives O(X^(1/3)log X). The standard Chebyshev prime-counting bound pi(y)=O(y/log y) gives A(X)=O(sqrt X/log X). The addition map from ordered proper-power pairs onto collision-supported targets gives |C(X)|<=A(X)^2. Dividing by the number of even targets proves density zero. Outside C(X), Q*Q(N)=0 exactly, so the corrected and uncorrected envelopes coincide.",
